{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels","id":1536185,"title":"Evil Angels?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-23T20:13:36-07:00","id":1536185,"title":"Evil Angels?","content":"So part of a backstory for an NPC character is basically a Captain Ahab situation where he inherits the Avatar (rating 5, with Past Lives 5) that, in the Dark Ages, suffered when a band of Inquisitors, with the help of an angel, killed his past incarnation\u2019s entire family and village, which was composed of pagans.<br /> <br /> So this angel haunts his nightmares, and his Avatar is determined to see it dead. Problem is, Angels are generally portrayed as good guys in Mage. Is there room for a godly, but evil, angel in the Astral Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T22:02:53-07:00","id":1536187,"title":"","content":"No. Had to type at least 10 characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T23:07:02-07:00","id":1536192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels#post1536185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So part of a backstory for an NPC character is basically a Captain Ahab situation where he inherits the Avatar (rating 5, with Past Lives 5) that, in the Dark Ages, suffered when a band of Inquisitors, with the help of an angel, killed his past incarnation\u2019s entire family and village, which was composed of pagans.<br /> <br /> So this angel haunts his nightmares, and his Avatar is determined to see it dead. Problem is, Angels are generally portrayed as good guys in Mage. Is there room for a godly, but evil, angel in the Astral Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure its called a demon.<br /> Also in the High umbra morality is very subjective. So something seen as good by a spirit does not have to be good via human standards or at least this human standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T02:42:33-07:00","id":1536195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels#post1536185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this angel haunts his nightmares, and his Avatar is determined to see it dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered making this angel another Avatar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T05:05:50-07:00","id":1536198,"title":"","content":"Someone with an honorable goal and a &quot;Utopia justifies the means&quot; worldview makes a great villain. Varys in &quot;Game of Thrones&quot; is focused on an old fashioned ideal &quot;a virtuous king will solve all of the realms problems.&quot; Towards this goal he murders honorable men, mutilates children, and weakens the realm for an invasion. An angel might be deluded into thinking that removing a few die hard pagans will aid in achieving a purer Christian kingdom. <br /> <br /> Give your Angel a noble goal and a warpped idea of how to achieve it. Marxist-Leninists set up brutal dictatorships to achieve an anarchist Utopia. Libertarians destroy social safety nets creating misery and poverty to secure liberty thus destroying the substance and possiblity of liberty for most people. Make your Angel equally deluded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T09:37:58-07:00","id":1536209,"title":"","content":"I am curious about the responses seemingly driven to absolve the concept of &quot;angel&quot; from any association with violence that our sensibilities would deem to be wrong. Particularly in light of how &quot;Biblically accurate angel&quot; had seemed to become a bit of a meme in the last couple of years.<br /> <br /> What would it be about Mage: the Ascension that would associate angels with some kind of objective standard of good, or at least only the palatable parts of a system of spirituality that are disconnected with the extent to which every single religion that professes a belief in angels has also displayed historical instances of willingness to commit disproportionate violence against people outside of their religious community (with scriptural citation)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T12:38:09-07:00","id":1536217,"title":"","content":"Yes. Duh. This is perfectly in line with the motivations of an angel from Christian mythology; it works as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T23:26:09-07:00","id":1536331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536217#post1536217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Duh. This is perfectly in line with the motivations of an angel from Christian mythology; it works as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;God's ways are not man's ways&quot;, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T23:30:11-07:00","id":1536332,"title":"","content":"Why are we assuming the Angel needs to be evil for this backstory to work?<br /> <br /> Maybe the PC's previous incarnation was just an asshole. And the angel was truly doing the righteous thing (or at least its part in it was righteous; the Inquisitors might have gone farther than the angel would have liked).<br /> <br /> The PC's Avatar, of course, may just harbor a grudge, even though its vessel deserved what they got. Just because it's an Avatar, doesn't mean it can't be in the wrong. Or just so resentful, it wants revenge, whether it's good or not. It's up to the PC/player to decide if they want to go along with that vendetta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T23:35:20-07:00","id":1536333,"title":"","content":"OH, OH, OH! I almost forgot!<br /> <br /> There's actually precedent for an &quot;Evil Angel&quot;, in Sorcerer: Revised. The patron Umbrood for the Order of the Golden Fly (militarized antisemites) is the angel that sent the plagues of Egypt from Exodus. And he hates Moses enough that he's willing to manipulate the Order (making them think they've bound him to service), in order to prosecute his own private war against the Jews.<br /> <br /> Verifiably, that angel is &quot;Evil&quot; by the estimation of the book, and aids and abets a villainous Sorcerer group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T08:30:03-07:00","id":1536364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536331#post1536331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;God's ways are not man's ways&quot;, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I read Revelations. Killing virtuous pagans is 100% consistent with the portrayal of God in Revelations, and it can be easily extrapolated from the emphasis on conversion in the rest of the New Testament (as well as commentary on it) that if a group of people are getting in the way of saving souls you ought to kill them. This has been mainstream Christian theology for quite some time (still is, in places) so it's a little weird to see people say that it won't work for an RPG game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T08:06:24-07:00","id":1536429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536364#post1536364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I read Revelations. Killing virtuous pagans is 100% consistent with the portrayal of God in Revelations, and it can be easily extrapolated from the emphasis on conversion in the rest of the New Testament (as well as commentary on it) that if a group of people are getting in the way of saving souls you ought to kill them. This has been mainstream Christian theology for quite some time (still is, in places) so it's a little weird to see people say that it won't work for an RPG game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be better to say that it is a mainstream opinion among Christians in a lot of times and places, rather than mainstream theology. Theologically, the goal is supposed to be conversion not killing, but history is full of great divides between what people claim to believe and how they actually act, and Christians are as susceptible to that as anyone. Indeed, that is a mainstream theological element of Christianity: that people will always fall short of what they should be.<br /> <br /> Indeed there's a great interchange between Napoleon and a Cardinal Ercole Consalvi. Napoleon threatened to crush the Catholic Church and the Cardinal responded: &quot;If in 1,800 years we clergy have failed to destroy the Church, do you really think that you'll be able to do it?&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the original question:<br /> <br /> There's plenty of room for an unfallen angel that pushes a lot of goals the PC thinks are evil. There's also room for an angel that thinks it is doing good and isn't, or a being that thinks it is an angel and isn't, like an Umbrood that is the human <i>idea</i> of an angel. If you want an actual angel that knows good and evil and chooses evil anyways, though, that pretty much has to be a demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T08:57:08-07:00","id":1536431,"title":"","content":"The point is that while a character, even an angel, may have an idea they see as objectively true of what Good and Evil are, this doesn't actually exist, maybe with the exception of bioethics (maybe).<br /> <br /> How do you define an angel to begin with? How this entity defines good? Is it even possible in Mage to have a definite answer to those questions? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> What I can agree at most is that any entity that understand the concept of an angel and thinks to be one, also does believe itself good, on whatever way it understands Good and Evil. Which still may signify the destruction of enemies of the Faith, if it sees such enemies as a threat greater than their chance at redemption/conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T10:51:35-07:00","id":1536446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536431#post1536431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that while a character, even an angel, may have an idea they see as objectively true of what Good and Evil are, this doesn't actually exist, maybe with the exception of bioethics (maybe).<br /> <br /> How do you define an angel to begin with? How this entity defines good? Is it even possible in Mage to have a definite answer to those questions? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> What I can agree at most is that any entity that understand the concept of an angel and thinks to be one, also does believe itself good, on whatever way it understands Good and Evil. Which still may signify the destruction of enemies of the Faith, if it sees such enemies as a threat greater than their chance at redemption/conversion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage's setting doesn't preclude objective good and evil, nor does it preclude an absolute creator. It is better for the themes of the setting if mages can't know for sure, but otherwise it is really up to each table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T13:28:16-07:00","id":1536465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536446#post1536446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage's setting doesn't preclude objective good and evil, nor does it preclude an absolute creator. It is better for the themes of the setting if mages can't know for sure, but otherwise it is really up to each table.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that <b>is</b> the point.<br /> <br /> There's no objective answers to those questions unless the ST decides there are, and even then the setting assumes those are unknowable, which may not be precluding them, but isn't too far from it.<br /> <br /> Even then, the ST can decide however they see fit. And in this case the ST has declared the intent to have an evil Angel, at least from their own POV, they just want to know if it is possible within the setting.<br /> <br /> Why on Earth should the possibility of making Angels objectively Good become an obligation to do so, even if the setting doesn't say such!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T20:23:35-07:00","id":1536478,"title":"","content":"I'd say Gabriel from the movie <i>Constantine</i> is an excellent example of an angel doing horrible things for what it believes to be good reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T21:54:28-07:00","id":1536480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536465#post1536465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why on Earth should the possibility of making Angels objectively Good become an obligation to do so, even if the setting doesn't say such!?</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s no obligation. I listed multiple alternatives, including an angel that is doing what it thinks is right but is wrong. That\u2019s not an objectively good angel. <br /> <br /> Indeed, an angel that knowingly chooses to do evil- that knows good and evil and chooses evil- that\u2019s also quite possible. It\u2019s just that there\u2019s already a term for that, and it is demon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T00:35:30-07:00","id":1536487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536465#post1536465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that <b>is</b> the point.<br /> <br /> There's no objective answers to those questions unless the ST decides there are, and even then the setting assumes those are unknowable, which may not be precluding them, but isn't too far from it.<br /> <br /> Even then, the ST can decide however they see fit. And in this case the ST has declared the intent to have an evil Angel, at least from their own POV, they just want to know if it is possible within the setting.<br /> <br /> Why on Earth should the possibility of making Angels objectively Good become an obligation to do so, even if the setting doesn't say such!?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are speaking in setting then acording to Demon the fallen there were angels on the side of the host that comited such atrocities that they were imprisoned in the abyss with the losing side.<br /> Im not sure i believe morality is subjective anymore. Does not mean we have a dnd aligment scale though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T03:12:18-07:00","id":1536490,"title":"","content":"I think it may help to shift the terms a little. Instead of 'good' I would switch to 'righteous'. Righteousness in a religious context means 'right in the eyes of God', and ties the very subjective terms of good and evil into the specific framework of that religion. Or in other words, morality is defined by the laws of God alone and the human perspective does not factor into it.<br /> <br /> I use this quite often for a character archetype I call Awful Good. Within their own morality, their actions may be completely justified, good, and without sin. To anyone outside of that morality, they appear like horrible zealots who commit heinous sins. So yeah, the people on the wrong end of an angel's <i>righteous </i>wrath would call it evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T12:12:58-07:00","id":1536519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536487#post1536487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we are speaking in setting then acording to Demon the fallen there were angels on the side of the host that comited such atrocities that they were imprisoned in the abyss with the losing side.<br /> Im not sure i believe morality is subjective anymore. Does not mean we have a dnd aligment scale though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>First, since we're discussing Mage we don't need to take DtF as a measure of what an Angel is, specially a medieval one.<br /> <br /> Second, I don't remember at all of any reference in DtF of angels in the side of God being imprisoned for any crime other than disobedience, can you cite the source?<br /> <br /> I can't say for sure that I read everything, but Demon is my fav splat and I clearly remember that both sides of the war committed atrocities aplenty, but punishment was solely based on obedience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T13:52:33-07:00","id":1536532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536519#post1536519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, since we're discussing Mage we don't need to take DtF as a measure of what an Angel is, specially a medieval one.<br /> <br /> Second, I don't remember at all of any reference in DtF of angels in the side of God being imprisoned for any crime other than disobedience, can you cite the source?<br /> <br /> I can't say for sure that I read everything, but Demon is my fav splat and I clearly remember that both sides of the war committed atrocities aplenty, but punishment was solely based on obedience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont remember, maybe i homebrewed that for my V5 like demon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T17:10:47-07:00","id":1536540,"title":"","content":"The distinction between Angels and Demons not being one of Good and Evil is one of the main staples of DtF. It's up to the ST if any side of the war is ultimately right or wrong, or even if an answer can be found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T10:33:13-07:00","id":1536673,"title":"","content":"First, you have to define &quot;Angel&quot;. Are you talking about the Elohim of Demon the Fallen, or the mental construction of the High Umbra? Because that are two different beings altogether. A being from the High Umbra is the concept of that being, so, a Angel from the High Umbra will not be evil, just because that is human morality. It is following the conceptual laws of god, and will act accordingly. It doesnt have a base to do &quot;evil&quot;, because is literally the concept of a servant of god (Can a animal be evil?), not a being with free will. The Elohim are a different beast entirily, because you can argue that they actually have Free Will, so yeah, a Elohim <i>can </i>be bad.<br /> <br /> This is a tangent, but im so fucking tired of the typical &quot;ACHTUALLY GOD IS BAD&quot;. Dude, do something more original","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T12:30:06-07:00","id":1536709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CamaradaDoppio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536673#post1536673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, you have to define &quot;Angel&quot;. Are you talking about the Elohim of Demon the Fallen, or the mental construction of the High Umbra? Because that are two different beings altogether. A being from the High Umbra is the concept of that being, so, a Angel from the High Umbra will not be evil, just because that is human morality. It is following the conceptual laws of god, and will act accordingly. It doesnt have a base to do &quot;evil&quot;, because is literally the concept of a servant of god (Can a animal be evil?), not a being with free will. The Elohim are a different beast entirily, because you can argue that they actually have Free Will, so yeah, a Elohim <i>can </i>be bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Banes can be evil--and they are; they may not have free will totally but they're acting with malice--I don't see why an angel would be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T08:54:18-07:00","id":1536985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536332#post1536332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are we assuming the Angel needs to be evil for this backstory to work?<br /> <br /> Maybe the PC's previous incarnation was just an asshole. And the angel was truly doing the righteous thing (or at least its part in it was righteous; the Inquisitors might have gone farther than the angel would have liked).<br /> <br /> The PC's Avatar, of course, may just harbor a grudge, even though its vessel deserved what they got. Just because it's an Avatar, doesn't mean it can't be in the wrong. Or just so resentful, it wants revenge, whether it's good or not. It's up to the PC/player to decide if they want to go along with that vendetta.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this approach. Let's not pretend that the &quot;pagans&quot; were innocent saints either. Plenty of Christians were the targets of human sacrifices at the hands of so called pagans - and I think we can all agree that, at least in today's era and age, human sacrifices are considered to be something &quot;bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe your previous incarnation was doing stuff that the culture considered to be absolutely fine - like sacrificing defect babies, or sending elders to a &quot;journey in the woods&quot;, which were practices that were absolutely common throughout human history over many cultures, and that would horrify medieval christians and modern audiences alike.<br /> <br /> Maybe the angel had a good reason to do what it did (whatever that &quot;angel&quot; might be).<br /> <br /> Biblically speaking, we have Sodom and Gomorrah who were so vile that they were cities filled with rapists and murderers (and it's implied that EVERYONE of those people were both), which I believe that everybody sane consider those to be the most heinous crimes possible along with sadistic torture.<br /> <br /> And in that story, the angels have no qualms about completely obliterating both cities, after failing to find even a single good person in them. The angels simply squash that den of inequity without any sort of moral pause.<br /> <br /> Considering JUST this context, could it be deemed to be a justified action? I think it would be hypocritical to say no. After, the world united in order to stop the genocidal Nazi Germany and Imperial Japan, who committed the most unspeakable atrocities imaginable. Was it right to bomb Germany and Japan into oblivion? I'd say that yes, it was absolutely moral to do so - including the 2 A bombs dropped on Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T09:03:05-07:00","id":1536986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CamaradaDoppio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536673#post1536673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a tangent, but im so fucking tired of the typical &quot;ACHTUALLY GOD IS BAD&quot;. Dude, do something more original</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Gnosticism 101. The &quot;God&quot; of WoD, the one that rewarded the obedient Elohim and cast aside the rebellious demons from DtF, this isn't the &quot;true God&quot;, but rather the Gnostic Demiurge (aka, roughly we could call him as &quot;The Devil&quot;).<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe entire &quot;mythology&quot; of WoD is distilled Gnosticism. That's why &quot;God is bad&quot;, is because he is not the &quot;real&quot; God, but rather the Demiurge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T10:29:54-07:00","id":1536992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536985#post1536985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this approach. Let's not pretend that the &quot;pagans&quot; were innocent saints either. Plenty of Christians were the targets of human sacrifices at the hands of so called pagans</div> </div> </div> </div>This basically never happened.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536986#post1536986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Gnosticism 101. The &quot;God&quot; of WoD, the one that rewarded the obedient Elohim and cast aside the rebellious demons from DtF, this isn't the &quot;true God&quot;, but rather the Gnostic Demiurge (aka, roughly we could call him as &quot;The Devil&quot;).<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200bThe entire &quot;mythology&quot; of WoD is distilled Gnosticism. That's why &quot;God is bad&quot;, is because he is not the &quot;real&quot; God, but rather the Demiurge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, this is bullshit. Gnosticism assumes that there is a true god but the Demiurge isn't it; that's not true in the World of Darkness. If there <i>is</i> a true monotheistic creator of the universe, it's God as usually described in Abrahamic theology (yes, including Christian sources; the World of Darkness is less anti-Semitic than a lot of Gnostic theology) and he's a dick; if there isn't then God is basically just a powerful spirit with delusions of grandeur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","user":"Citrakayah","date":". 06-08-2024, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:04:28-07:00","id":1536994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536992#post1536992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This basically never happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>D:tF basically had that happen at the direction of the Earthbound, I think. Not really its best moment, even considering that Down to Fuck has had a lot of bad moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:12:15-07:00","id":1536996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536994#post1536994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> D:tF basically had that happen at the direction of the Earthbound, I think. Not really its best moment, even considering that Down to Fuck has had a lot of bad moments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean in real life. I don't really like how the response to this NPC's backstory having Christians fanatics massacre pagans and asking us if it's possible for there to be an evil angel in WoD cosmology has turned into &quot;wah, I don't like that my favored religion which historically killed a ton of people might be portrayed negatively in a campaign' and 'but what if the pagans deserved it though?' Seriously, that's just gross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","user":"Citrakayah","date":". 06-08-2024, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:29:41-07:00","id":1536999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536985#post1536985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in that story, the angels have no qualms about completely obliterating both cities, after failing to find even a single good person in them. The angels simply squash that den of inequity without any sort of moral pause.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are missing the point, imo. Acting righteous is devoid of considerations of morality or justice for the actor.<br /> <br /> If God tells you to go from door to door and murder every firstborn, you can do so without moral consideration because God is the highest moral authority, so acting amoral on his word is impossible by definition - even if your personal moral compass tells you otherwise.<br /> <br /> That's exactly why worldly arms of religions and secular governments throw out their deus vults and mashallahs to whip people into slaughter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536985#post1536985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it right to bomb Germany and Japan into oblivion? I'd say that yes, it was absolutely moral to do so - including the 2 A bombs dropped on Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremendously horrible choice for an example, but maybe it serves to illustrate the point here: I'm assuming - or at least I hope - that your personal morality would categorize killing innocents as morally wrong. But you are willing to suspend your moral conflict in this, because you believe the actions of what you perceive as a higher moral authority (in this case the Allies) were righteous.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T13:45:10-07:00","id":1537029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536999#post1536999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are missing the point, imo. Acting righteous is devoid of considerations of morality or justice for the actor.<br /> <br /> If God tells you to go from door to door and murder every firstborn, you can do so without moral consideration because God is the highest moral authority, so acting amoral on his word is impossible by definition - even if your personal moral compass tells you otherwise.<br /> <br /> That's exactly why worldly arms of religions and secular governments throw out their deus vults and mashallahs to whip people into slaughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRL, it's also not something that Christianity or Judaism accept: \u201cif you're sure God is telling you to do it, then it is by definition moral\u201d is, in fact, an Islamic belief, whereas Christians and Jews add a layer to that of \u201cGod has told us what he considers to be good and evil; and if you think that God is telling you to do something that he has said is evil, don't listen; you're being deceived.\u201d<br /> <br /> But again, that's IRL. The World of Darkness deviates from that. In MtA, moral uncertainty is cranked up to 11 such that anyone who claims to know for certain is <i>probably</i> wrong \u2014 about the certainly, at least. It's not that there <i>isn't </i>an absolute truth, such as am absolute morality; only that nobody can be <i>sure </i>that what they think is true actually is.<br /> <br /> And to me, that uncertainty is part of the horror of MtA.<br /> <br /> This isn't a DtF forum; but since it's was brought up, the DtF position on this is that God is literally <i>dead: </i>not in the philosophical sense that people have abandoned belief in God, but in the sense that shortly after God created the universe, God <i>ceased to exist. </i>The angels have been acting in their own ever since, attempting to implement <i>what they believe would have been </i>God's will if He were still around.<br /> <br /> VtM takes yet <i>another</i> route, where God exists and is a jerk; though that <i>is </i>compatible with the notion that what the vampire <i>think of </i>as God is in fact what Gnosticism identifies as the Demiurge.<br /> <br /> I don't go as far as Magus Maximus does in claiming that the World of Darkness is distilled Gnosticism; but there are certainly elements throughout the setting that are <i>compatible with</i> Gnostic beliefs.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> With all that said: if you want to portray an actual evil angel, there's support for that in the World of Darkness. I'm not inclined to, as it's becoming a tired cliche; But I'm not running your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Typo 06-10-2024, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T16:56:27-07:00","id":1537046,"title":"","content":"There are many ways to consider morality depending on where you are on complexity scale:<br /> 1. Hes bad cause i dont like it - primitive and shallow, self centered.<br /> 2. Hes bad cause morality is objective - focused on your culture circle version of morality.<br /> 3. Morality is subjective and we cant judge someone with our measure - very compasionate but a bit misguided.<br /> 4. All humans are capable of good and evil and we should judge them by their actions of where and when they take place - a fair more harmonic way of looking on things.<br /> <br /> Question is do we see an Angel a more enlightened or primitive being when it comes to self reflection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T21:07:37-07:00","id":1537057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536996#post1536996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean in real life. I don't really like how the response to this NPC's backstory having Christians fanatics massacre pagans and asking us if it's possible for there to be an evil angel in WoD cosmology has turned into &quot;wah, I don't like that my favored religion which historically killed a ton of people might be portrayed negatively in a campaign' and 'but what if the pagans deserved it though?' Seriously, that's just gross.</div> </div> </div> </div>Human sacrifice is well documented throughout history! And widely disseminated too! The cult of Bacchus in ancient Greece for instance had instances of cannibalism!<br /> <br /> First and foremost, I'm an atheist my friend, so don't come up with this idiotic nonsense about &quot;your favorite religion&quot;. All religions to me are delusional silliness, including Christianity.<br /> <br /> That does NOT however excludes the idiotic nonsense from OTHER religions. And yes, all things considered, Christianity ranks up waaaaaaaaaay up on top at the scale of morally good and for a positive impact in the world. Compare it to the gods of Rome and it's not even close. Rome was absolutely atrocious, tyrannical and violent. Christianity was a HUGE major moral upgrade for Rome. It introduced among others the idea of individuality, which NEVER existed anywhere else.<br /> <br /> The Norse mythology is rich and intriguing, but they were brutal and savage, a religion based on worshipping war and violence (something they had in common with the Romans by the way). And yes, there are also many stances of human sacrifices too.<br /> <br /> But by far, the worse religions of all, the most detestable and violent, were socialism, the Aztec paganism and Islam, in that order. Those are the 3 most inhumane ideologies that ever plagued humanity, Christianism doesn't even come close<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T22:52:34-07:00","id":1537061,"title":"","content":"I am a Nietzschenian however, and while I do believe Christianism is better than most, I adhere to Nietzsche's idea that Christianism is a slave morality - a religion created by slaves, for slaves and to slaves.<br /> <br /> As such, it is a religion that breeds mediocrity and that tries to suffocate any sort of individual excellency, and that's extremely detrimental.<br /> <br /> Christianism was the &quot;woke movement&quot; of ancient Rome. No wonder that such virulent ideologies such as communism or its modern day incarnation of it - wokeism - comes from the Western World. The cult of achievement and individual excellency can only be born from a &quot;master morality&quot;. Slave morality is pathologically driven towards equality - hence why Marxist ideas could only ever come from a Christian background.<br /> <br /> We need a middle ground between the 2. Master morality is great at cultivating strength and inducing greatness, but it comes at the cost of simply squashing the weak as insects because they are &quot;not worthy&quot;, just like in ancient Rome, were everybody were a slave to the State (even the non slaves were just mere fuel for the legions). Slave morality on the other hand, while placing huge value over everyone, can't stand individuals that stand above the others.<br /> <br /> We need to cultivate the good side of both - value all life, but admiring personal accomplishments - while rejecting the bad sides of both.<br /> <br /> I do say that Christianism marked a massive change throughout human morality, and a positive change, but it is NOT the final answer, for it is deeply flawed, and it seems to have finally run its course, or as Nietzsche said, we live in the era of the &quot;Last Men&quot;, which breeds mediocre weaklings incapable of dealing with life. In that sense, Christianity and its silly message of just being a lamb to the slaughter, has failed us.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T23:10:12-07:00","id":1537062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536999#post1536999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Tremendously horrible choice for an example, but maybe it serves to illustrate the point here: I'm assuming - or at least I hope - that your personal morality would categorize killing innocents as morally wrong. But you are willing to suspend your moral conflict in this, because you believe the actions of what you perceive as a higher moral authority (in this case the Allies) were righteous.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are no innocents in war. That's just silly. At the end of the day, we live in a jungle fighting for survival, and in the end of the day, it will ALWAYS boil down to &quot;either my tribe's survival or my enemy tribe's survival&quot;.<br /> <br /> Our moral codes are just a comfortable veneer of civilization that we build around ourselves so that we can look at the mirror without having to deal with the fact that we are savage barbarians and that we would happily plunge an axe in our neighbors faces if the food that comes everyday into our supermarkets were suddenly over.<br /> <br /> We build those superstructures that we call &quot;civilization&quot; as a collective effort and that allows for us to behave in such &quot;civilized&quot; manners because it is to our own benefit.<br /> <br /> But let it all collapse, and we turn into murderers and thieves basically instantly.<br /> <br /> The Germans and the Japanese were two hordes of blood thirsty barbaric savages, and if they had won, we would probably be their slaves if lucky, or most likely, their victims.<br /> <br /> The bombings of Dresden and Berlin and the bombings of Tokyo killed way more people than the 2 atomic bombs. Were they justified? HELL YES.<br /> <br /> WW2 was a total war of extermination. In such a context, we must drop such naive concepts such as &quot;morality&quot;. It is a matter of survival. If I have to choose between me to live and you to die, or between you to live and me to die, than I'll kill you 1000 times before letting you kill me once. It really is that simple.<br /> <br /> In fact, the Germans and the Japanese should kiss the fear of the allies throughout all of eternity for the mere fact that they still exist. In less enlightened times - which would mean, most of human history - after everything that they have done, the winners would simply slaughter every single one of them down to the last child. Like Rome did to Carthage for example.<br /> <br /> So, war is not the best place for you to request moral behavior, because war is when we humans regress towards our most basic animal drives, and war is a struggle for survival, upon which being defeated can literally mean the total obliteration of an entire population, particularly in a total war of extermination such as WW2 was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T03:38:56-07:00","id":1537067,"title":"","content":"Magus, I'm not going to engage with that mire of misconceptions any further, but I urge you to carefully re-read what Nietzsche wrote about reconstructing personal morality after deconstructing it. Maybe with some annotations or secondary literature.<br /> <br /> <br /> I apologize for dragging the conversation off-topic, and refer to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>'s answer as it reflects my own opinions on the original question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T07:26:10-07:00","id":1537150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536185-evil-angels?p=1536996#post1536996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean in real life. I don't really like how the response to this NPC's backstory having Christians fanatics massacre pagans and asking us if it's possible for there to be an evil angel in WoD cosmology has turned into &quot;wah, I don't like that my favored religion which historically killed a ton of people might be portrayed negatively in a campaign' and 'but what if the pagans deserved it though?' Seriously, that's just gross.</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't. Going back through the thread, I don't see anyone saying Christians didn't kill pagans and anyone other than Magus asking if the pagans deserved it. The closest was my own comment that the Christians weren't supposed to be doing that, but I certainly didn't claim they didn't. The backstory discussion has largely been over the theology of the angel not the historical accuracy of the people.<br /> <br /> As you say, the OP asked if it was possible to have a godly, evil angel in Mage. Presumably one in line with Christian theology based on context. If those are hard restrictions, the answer is no. If we area allowed to fudge things a little (and we usually are in Mage), the answer is yes. And indeed, there've been a lot of good suggestions about how to fudge things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T16:40:24-07:00","id":1537178,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Please keep the framing to the original question and avoid attacks on religions or treatises on the darker impulses of human nature.</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> The short answer is &quot;if it works at your table, go for it.&quot; Reality is subjective in mage.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}